{
  "title": "Munajaat al Shabaniyyah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "It is recommended to say the following confidential prayer (Munaajaat) that has been narrated by Ibn Khalawayh who commented on it, saying, “This is the confidential prayer of Imam Ali Ameer al-Momineen and the Holy Imams (a.s.) who used to say it in the month of Sha’ban.”\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَ اسْمَعْ دُعَآئِيْ اِذَا دَعَوْتُكَ\nWAS MA’ DO-A’AA-EE EZAA DA-A’WTOKA\nYou listen to my supplication whenever I pray to you,\nوَ اسْمَعْ نِدَآئِيْٓ اِذَا نَادَيْتُكَ\nWAS MA’ NEDAAA-EE EZAA NAADAYTOKA\nlisten to my call whenever I call upon you,\nوَ اَقْبِلْ عَلَيَّ اِذَا نَاجَيْتُكَ\nWA AQBIL A’LAYYA EZAA NAAJAYTOKA\nand accept from me whenever I make my submission to you in confidence,\nفَقَدْ هَرَبْتُ اِلَيْكَ\nFAQAD HARABTO ELAYKA\nI have escaped towards you and stood before you,\nوَ وَقَفْتُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nWA WAQAFTO BAYNA YADAYKA\nstanding before You, \nمُسْتَكِيْنًا لَكَ\nMUSTAKEENAN LAKA\nshowing submission to You,\nمُتَضَرِّعًا اِلَيْكَ\nMOTAZARRE-A’N ELAYKA\nimploring You,\nرَاجِيًا لِمَا لَدَيْكَ ثَوَابِيْ\nRAAJEYAN LEMAA LADAYKA SAWAABEE\nand hoping for the reward that You have for me.\nوَ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِيْ نَفْسِيْ\nWA TA’LAMO MAA FEE NAFSEE\nYou know what is in my inner self,\nوَ تَخْبُرُ حَاجَتِيْ\nWA TAKHBORO HAAJATEE\nand you are aware of my needs,\nوَ تَعْرِفُ ضَمِيْرِيْ\nWA TA’REFO ZAMEEREE\nand You know what is in my conscience,\nوَ لَا يَخْفٰى عَلَيْكَ اَمْرُ مُنْقَلَبِيْ وَ مَثْوَايَ\nWA LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYKA AMRO MUNQALABEE WA MASWAAYA\nand all my moves and stillness are known by You.\nوَ مَآ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُبْدِءَ بِهٖ مِنْ مَنْطِقِيْ\nWA MAA OREEDO AN UBDE-A BEHI MIN MANTEQEE\nSo are all the utterances which I want to begin with,\nوَ اَتَفَوَّهُ بِهٖ مِنْ طَلِبَتِيْ\nWA ATAFAWWAHO BEHI MIN TALEBATEE\nall the requests that I want to express,\nوَ اَرْجُوْهُ لِعَاقِبَتِيْ\nWA ARJOOHO LE-A’AQEBATEE\nand all the expectation that I hope for my future.\nوَ قَدْ جَرَتْ مَقَادِيْرُكَ عَلَيَّ يَا سَيِّدِيْ\nWA QAD JARAT MAQAADEEROKA A’LAYYA YAA SAYYEDEE\nO my Master, all Your decisions in relation to me have come to pass\nفِيْمَا يَكُوْنُ مِنِّيْٓ اِلٰٓى اٰخِرِ عُمْرِيْ\nFEEMAA YAKOONO MINNEE ELAA AAKHERE U’MREE\nin all that happens to me up to the end of my life,\nمِنْ سَرِيْرَتِيْ وَ عَلَانِيَتِيْ\nMIN SAREERATEE WA A’LAANEYATEE\nincluding my secret and open matters, shall be experienced by me.\nوَ بِيَدِكَ لَا بِيَدِ غَيْرِكَ زِيَادَتِيْ وَ نَقْصِيْ\nWA BE-YADEKAGHAYREKA ZEYAADATEE WA NAQSEE\nAnd it is in Your hands, not anybody else’s, that are all my gains and losses\nوَ نَفْعِيْ وَ ضَرِّيْٓ\nWA NAF-E’E WA ZARREE\nand all the benefits and harms that come upon me.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ حَرَمْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِيْ يَرْزُقُنِيْ\nELAAHEE IN HARAMTANEE FAMAN ZAL LAZEE YARZOQONEE\nMy Lord, if You deprive me (of Your sustenance), then who else can ever provide me with sustenance?\nوَ اِنْ خَذَلْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِيْ يَنْصُرُنِيْ.\nWA IN KHAZALTANEE FAMAN ZAL LAZEE YANSORONEE\nIf You forsake me, then who else will help me?\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ غَضَبِكَ\nELAAHEE A-O’OZO BEKA MIN GHAZABEKA\nMy Lord, I do seek Your protection against Your wrath \nوَ حُلُوْلِ سَخَطِكَ\nWA HOLOOLE SAKHATEKA\nand earning your displeasure.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ كُنْتُ غَيْرَ مُسْتَأْهِلٍ لِرَحْمَتِكَ\nELAAHEE IN KUNTO GHAYRA MUSTAAHELIN LE-RAHMATEKA\nO my Lord, if I am not deserving of Your mercy,\nفَاَنْتَ اَهْلٌ اَنْ تَجُوْدَ عَلَيَّ بِفَضْلِ سَعَتِكَ\nFA-ANTA AHLUN AN TAJOODA A’LAYYA BE-FAZLE SA-A’TEKA\nYou are certainly fit to be generous to me by virtue of your magnanimity.\nاِلٰهِيْ كَاَنِّيْ بِنَفْسِيْ وَاقِفَةٌ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nELAAHEE KA-ANNEE BE-NAFSEE WAAQEFATUN BAYNA YADAYKA\nMy Lord, its like I see myself standing before You\nوَ قَدْ اَظَلَّهَا حُسْنُ تَوَكُّلِيْ عَلَيْكَ\nWA QAD AZALLAHAA HUSNO TAWAKKOLEE A’LAYKA\nIt has been shaded by the goodness of my trust in you\nفَقُلْتَ مَآ اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ وَ تَغَمَّدْتَنِيْ بِعَفْوِكَ\nFAQULTO MAA ANTA AHLOHU WA TAGHAMMAD-TANEE BE-A’FWEKA\nYou said what befitted You and sheltered me with your forgiveness.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ عَفَوْتَ فَمَنْ اَوْلٰى مِنْكَ بِذٰلِكَ\nELAAHEE IN A’FAWTA FAMAN AWLAA MINKA BE-ZAALEKA\nMy Lord, if you pardon me, then who else is worthier than You are in pardoning.\nوَ اِنْ كَانَ قَدْ دَنَا اَجَلِيْ\nWA IN KAANA QAD DANAA AJALEE\nIf my time of death is near \nوَ لَمْ يُدْنِنِيْ مِنْكَ عَمَلِيْ\nWA LAM YUDNENEE MINKA A’MALEE\nand my deeds have not brought me close to You\nفَقَدْ جَعَلْتُ الْاِقْرَارَ بِالذَّنْبِ اِلَيْكَ وَسِيْلَتِيْٓ\nFAQAD JA-A’LTUL IQRAARA BIZ-ZANBE ELAYKA WASEELATEE\nI make this confession of my sins to be a means of approaching You.\nاِلٰهِيْ قَدْ جُرْتُ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ فِيْ النَّظَرِ لَهَا\nELAAHEE QAD JURTO A’LAA NAFSEE FIN NAZARE LAHAA\nMy Lord, I have been unjust to my soul for I have not looked after it; \nفَلَهَا الْوَيْلُ اِنْ لَمْ تَغْفِرْ لَهَآ\nFALAHAL WAYLO IN LAM TAGHFIR LAHAA\nIt will be doomed if You do not forgive me.\nاِلٰهِيْ لَمْ يَزَلْ بِرُّكَ عَلَيَّ اَيَّامَ حَيَاتِيْ\nELAAHEE LAM YAZAL BIRROKA A’LAYYA AYYAAMA HAYAATEE\nMy Lord, You have never ceased Your favors from me all my lifetime;\nفَلَا تَقْطَعْ بِرَّكَ عَنِّيْ فِيْ مَمَاتِيْٓ\nFALAA TAQ-TA’ BERRAKA A’NNEE FEE MAMAATEE\nSo do not cease Your goodness towards me at the time of my death.\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ اٰيَسُ مِنْ حُسْنِ نَظَرِكَ لِيْ بَعْدَ مَمَاتِيْ\nELAAHEE KAYFA AAYASO MIN HUSNE NAZAREKA LEE BA’DA MAMAATEE\nMy Lord, how can I despair of Your benevolent attention towards me after my death\nوَ اَنْتَ لَمْ تُوَلِّنِيْٓ اِلَّا الْجَمِيْلَ فِيْ حَيَاتِيْ\nWA ANTA LAM TOWALLENEE ILLAL JAMEELA FEE HAYAATEE\nwhile You have always been good to me throughout my lifetime?\nاِلٰهِيْ تَوَلَّ مِنْ اَمْرِيْ مَآ اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ\nELAAHEE TAWALLA MIN AMREE MAA ANTA AHLOHU\nMy Lord, (please) manage my affairs in the very way that befits You,\nوَ عُدْ عَلَيَّ بِفَضْلِكَ عَلٰى مُذْنِبٍ قَدْ غَمَرَهُ جَهْلُهٗ\nWA U’D A’LAYYA BE-FAZLEKA A’LAA MUZNEBIN QAD GHAMARAHU JAHLOHU\nand confer upon me—a sinful person who is covered by his ignorance—with Your favors.\nاِلٰهِيْ قَدْ سَتَرْتَ عَلَيَّ ذُنُوْبًا فِيْ الدُّنْيَا\nELAAHEE QAD SATARTA A’LAYYA ZONOOBAN FID DUNYAA\nMy Lord, You have concealed my sins in this world,\nوَ اَنَآ اَحْوَجُ اِلٰى سَتْرِهَا عَلَيَّ مِنْكَ فِي الْاُخْرٰى\nWA ANAA AHWAJO ELAA SATREHAA A’LAYYA MINKA FIL UKHRAA\nbut I am in greater need of their being concealed in the Next Life.\nاِلٰهِيْ قَدْ اَحْسَنْتَ اِلَيَّ\nELAAHEE QAD AHSANTA ELAYYA\nYou have not revealed my sins \nاِذْ لَمْ تُظْهِرْهَا لِاَحَدٍ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nIZ LAM TUZHIRHAA LE-AHADIN MIN E’BAADEKAS SAALEHEEN\neven before any of Your righteous servants;\nفَلَا تَفْضَحْنِيْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ عَلٰى رُؤُسِ الْاَشْهَادِ\nFALAA TAFZAHNEE YAWMAL QEYAAMATE A’LAA RO-OOSIL ASHHAADE\ntherefore, (please) do not humuliate me on the Resurrection Day before all the witnesses.\nاِلٰهِيْ جُوْدُكَ بَسَطَ اَمَلِيْ\nELAAHEE JOODOKA BASATA AMALEE\nMy Lord, it is Your magnanimity that expanded my hope,\nوَ عَفْوُكَ اَفْضَلُ مِنْ عَمَلِيْ\nWA A’FWOKA AFZALO MIN A’MALEE\nand surely Your pardon is superior to my deeds.\nاِلٰهِيْ فَسُرَّنِيْ بِلِقَآئِكَ يَوْمَ تَقْضِيْ فِيْهِ بَيْنَ عِبَادِكَ\nELAAHEE FASURRANEE BELEQAAA-EKA YAWMA TAQZEE FEEHE BAYNA E’BAADEKA\nMy Lord, therefore gladden my heart when I meet You on the day when You shall judge between Your servants.\nاِلٰهِيْ اِعْتِذَارِيْٓ اِلَيْكَ اعْتِذَارُ مَنْ لَمْ يَسْتَغْنِ عَنْ قَبُوْلِ عُذْرِهٖ\nELAAHEE E-A’TEZAAREE ELAYKA’ TEZAARO MAN LAM YASTAGHNE A’N QABOOLE U’ZREHI\nMy Lord, I submit to You the apology of one who cannot dispense with the acceptance of his excuse;\nفَاقْبَلْ عُذْرِيْ يَآ اَكْرَمَ مَنِ اعْتَذَرَ اِلَيْهِ الْمُسِيْٓئُوْنَ.\nFAQBAL U’ZREE YAA AKRAMA MANE’ TAZARA ELAYHIL MOSEE-OONA.\nso, (please) accept my excuse, O most Magnanimous of all those before whom the guilty make an apology.\nاِلٰهِيْ لَا تَرُدُّ حَاجَتِيْ\nELAAHEE LAA TARUDA HAAJATEE\nMy Lord, (please) do not reject my request,\nوَ لَا تُخَيِّبْ طَمَعِيْ\nWA LAA TOKHAYYIB TAMA-E’E\ndo not disappoint my hope for You,\nوَ لَا تَقْطَعْ مِنْكَ رَجَآئِيْ وَ اَمَلِيْٓ\nWA LAA TAQTA’ MINKA RAJAAA-EE WA AMALEE\nand do not cut off from You my hope and expectations from You.\nاِلٰهِيْ لَوْ اَرَدْتَ هَوَانِيْ لَمْ تَهْدِنِيْ\nELAAHEE LAW ARADTA HAWAANEE LAM TAHDENEE\nMy Lord, had You wanted to humiliate me, You would not have guided me (to You).\nوَ لَوْ اَرَدْتَ فَضِيْحَتِيْ لَمْ تُعَافِنِيْٓ\nWA LAW ARADTA FAZEEHATEE LAM TO-A’AFENEE\nHad You decided to humiliate me,You would not have excused me.\nاِلٰهِيْ مَا اَظُنُّكَ تَرُدُّنِيْ فِيْ حَاجَةٍ قَدْ اَفْنَيْتُ عُمْرِيْ فِيْ طَلَبِهَا مِنْكَ\nELAAHEE MAA AZUNNOKA TARUDDANEE FEE HAAJATIN QAD AFNAYTO U’MREE FEE TALABEHAA MINKA\nMy Lord, I do not expect You to reject my request that I spent my whole lifetime asking for it from You.\nاِلٰهِيْ فَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ اَبَدًا اَبَدًا دَآئِمًا سَرْمَدًا\nELAAHEE FALAKAL HAMDO ABADAN ABADAN DAAA-EMAN SARMADAN\nMy Lord, all praise be to You, forever, forever, perpetually, everlastingly,\nيَزِيْدُ وَ لَا يَبِيْدُ كَمَا تُحِبُّ وَ تَرْضٰىٓ\nYAZEEDO WA LAA YABEEDO KAMAA TOHIBBO WA TARZAA\nincreasingly, and imperishably, as exactly as You like and please.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ اَخَذْتَنِيْ بِجُرْمِيْٓ اَخَذْتُكَ بِعَفْوِكَ\nELAAHEE IN AKHAZTANEE BEJURMEE AKHAZTOKA BE-A’FWEKA\nMy Lord, if You punish me for my offense, I shall cling to Your pardon,\nوَ اِنْ اَخَذْتَنِيْ بِذُنُوْبِيْٓ اَخَذْتُكَ بِمَغْفِرَتِكَ\nWA IN AKHAZTANEE BE-ZONOOBEE AKHAZTOKA BEMAGHFERATEKA\nif You cease me for my sins, I shall take hold of Your forgiveness,\nوَ اِنْ اَدْخَلْتَنِيْ النَّارَ اَعْلَمْتُ اَهْلَهَآ اَنِّيْٓ اُحِبُّكَ\nWA IN ADKHALTANIN NAARA A-A’LAMTO AHLAHAA ANNEE OHIBBOKA\nand if You put me to the fire, I shall declare to its inmates that I love You.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ كَانَ صَغُرَ فِيْ جَنْبِ طَاعَتِكَ عَمَلِيْ\nELAAHEE IN KAANA SAGHORA FEE JANBE TAA-A’TEKA A’MALEE\nMy Lord, should my deeds be insignificant with respect to obedience to You,\nفَقَدْ كَبُرَ فِيْ جَنْبِ رَجَآئِكَ اَمَلِيْٓ\nFAQAD KABORA FEE JANBE RAJAAA-EKA AMALEE\nGreat indeed is my hope with respect to my expectations from You.\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ اَنْقَلِبُ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ بِالْخَيْبَةِ مَحْرُوْمًا\nELAAHEE KAYFA ANQALEBO MIN I’NDEKA BIL-KHAYBATE MAHROOMAN\nMy Lord, how can it be that I return from You with disappointment and deprivation\nوَ قَدْ كَانَ حُسْنُ ظَنِّيْ بِجُوْدِكَ اَنْ تَقْلِبَنِيْ بِالنَّجَاةِ مَرْحُوْمًا\nWA QAD KAANA HUSNO ZANNEE BEJOODEKA AN TAQLEBANEE BIN-NAJAATE MARHOOMAN\nfor indeed my beautiful opinion about Your generosity was that You shall reverse my fate by saving me mercifully.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ قَدْ اَفْنَيْتُ عُمُرِيْ فِيْ شِرَّةِ السَّهْوِ عَنْكَ\nELAAHEE WA QAD AFNAYTO O’MOREE FEE SHIRRATIS SAHWE A’NKA\nMy Lord, I have spent my entire lifetime in being negligent to You\nوَ اَبْلَيْتُ شَبَابِيْ فِيْ سَكْرَةِ التَّبَاعُدِ مِنْكَ\nWA ABLAYTO SHABAABEE FEE SAKRATIT TABAA-O’DE MINKA\nand I have spent my whole youth with the stupor of being distant from You.\nاِلٰهِيْ فَلَمْ اَسْتَيْقِظْ اَيَّامَ اغْتِرَارِيْ بِكَ\nELAAHEE FALAM ASTAYQIZ AYYAAMAGH TERAAREE BEKA\nMy Lord, I did not wake up from my delusions\nوَ رُكُوْنِيْٓ اِلٰى سَبِيْلِ سَخَطِكَ.\nWA ROKOONEE ELAA SABEELE SAKHATEKA.\nand did not desist from pursuing the path of Your displeasure.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ اَنَا عَبْدُكَ وَ ابْنُ عَبْدِكَ قَآئِمٌ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nELAAHEE WA ANAA A’BDOKA WAB NO A’BDEKA QAAA-EMUN BAYNA YADAYKA\nMy Lord, nevertheless, I am—Your servant and the son of Your servant, now standing before You\nمُتَوَسِّلٌ بِكَرَمِكَ اِلَيْكَ\nMOTAWASSELUN BEKARAMEKA ELAYKA\nand begging You in the name of Your generosity.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اَنَا عَبْدٌ اَتَنَصَّلُ اِلَيْكَ مِمَّا كُنْتُ اُوَاجِهُكَ بِهٖ\nELAAHEE ANAA A’BDUN ATANASSALO ELAYKA MIMMAA KUNTO OWAAJEHOKA BEHI\nMy Lord, I am a servant, disavowing before You\nمِنْ قِلَّةِ اسْتِحْيَآئِيْ مِنْ نَظَرِكَ\nMIN QILLATIS TEHYAA-EE MIN NAZAREKA\nof my past attitude of lack of shame in Your sight\nوَ اَطْلُبُ الْعَفْوَ مِنْكَ اِذِ الْعَفْوُ نَعْتٌ لِكَرَمِكَ\nWA ATLOBUL A’FWA MINKA EZIL A’FWO NA’TUN LEKARAMEKA\nseek Your pardon as it is the attribute of Your magnanimty to pardon;\nاِلٰهِيْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لِيْ حَوْلٌ فَاَنْتَقِلَ بِهٖ عَنْ مَعْصِيَتِكَ\nELAAHEE LAM YAKUN LEE HAWLUN FA-ANTAQEKA BEHI A’N MA’SEYATEKA\nMy Lord, I had no strength to desist from Your disobedience\nاِلَّا فِيْ وَقْتٍ اَيْقَظْتَنِيْ لِمَحَبَّتِكَ\nILLAA FEE WAQTIN AYQAZTANEE LEMAHABBATEKA\nexcept when You awakened me for Your love\nوَ كَمَآ اَرَدْتَ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ كُنْتُ\nWA KAMAAA ARADTA AN AKOONA KUNTO\nHence, I desired, that I become exactly as You want me to be.\nفَشَكَرْتُكَ بِاِدْخَالِيْ فِيْ كَرَمِكَ\nFASHAKARTOKA BE-IDKHAALEE FEE KARAMEKA\nI have thus thanked You, for You admitting me into Your generosity\nوَ لِتَطْهِيْرِ قَلْبِيْ مِنْ اَوْسَاخِ الْغَفْلَةِ عَنْكَ\nWA LE-TATHEERE QALBEE MIN AWSAAKHIL GHAFLATE A’NKA\nand You have purified my heart from the filth of being inattentive to You.\nاِلٰهِيْ انْظُرْ اِلَيَّ نَظَرَ مَنْ نَادَيْتَهٗ فَاَجَابَكَ\nELAAHIN ZUR ELAYYA MAN NAADAYTAHU FA-AJAABAKA\nMy Lord, (please) look upon me in the same way as You have looked at one whom You called and he has responded to You\nوَ اسْتَعْمَلْتَهٗ بِمَعُوْنَتِكَ فَاَطَاعَكَ\nWAS TA’MALTAHU BE-MA-O’ONATEKA FA-ATAA-A’KA\nand whom You used him in Your service with Your aid and so he obeys You.\nيَا قَرِيْبًا لَا يَبْعُدُ عَنِ الْمُغْتَرِّ بِهٖ\nYAA QAREEBAN LAA YAB-O’DO A’NIL MUGHTARRE BEHI\nO the Near one who is not far away from those who love Him ardently\nوَ يَا جَوَادًا لَا يَبْخَلُ عَمَّنْ رَجَا ثَوَابَهٗ\nWA YAA JAWAADAN LAA YABKHALO A’MMAN RAJAA SAWAABAHU\nO He Who is too magnanimous to deprive one who hopes for His reward!\nاِلٰهِيْ هَبْ لِيْ قَلْبًا يُدْنِيْهِ مِنْكَ شَوْقُهٗ\nELAAHEE HAB LEE QALBAN YUDNEEHE MINKA SHAWQOHU\nMy Lord, (please) grant me a heart whose longing for You will draw one close to You,\nوَ لِسَانًا يُرْفَعُ اِلَيْكَ صِدْقُهٗ\nWA LESAANAN YURFA-O’ ELAYKA SIDQOHU\na tongue whose truthfulness ascends towards You,\nوَ نَظَرًا يُقَرِّبُهٗ مِنْكَ حَقُّهٗ\nWA NAZARAN YOQARREBOHU MINKA HAQQOHU\nand a sight whose trueness brings it close to You.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنَّ مَنْ تَعَرَّفَ بِكَ غَيْرُ مَجْهُوْلٍ\nELAAHEE INNA MAN TA-A’RRAFA BEKA GHAYRO MAJHOOLIN\nMy Lord, certainly he who recognizes You shall never be anonymous,\nوَ مَنْ لَاذَ بِكَ غَيْرُ مَخْذُوْلٍ\nWA MAN LAAZABEKA GHAYRO MAKHZOOLIN\nhe who seeks Your shelter shall never be disappointed,\nوَ مَنْ اَقْبَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ غَيْرُ مَمْلُوْكٍ.\nWA MAN AQBALTA A’LAYHE GHAYRO MAMLOOKIN.\nand he to whom You turn to does not fall victim to servility (dejection).\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنَّ مَنِ انْتَهَجَ بِكَ لَمُسْتَنِيْرٌ\nELAAHEE INNA MANIN TAHAJA BEKA LA-MUSTANEERUN\nMy Lord, certainly he who abides by Your Path shall be enlightened,\nوَ اِنَّ مَنِ اعْتَصَمَ بِكَ لَمُسْتَجِيْرٌ\nWA INNA MANE’ TASAMA BEKA LAMUSTAJEERUN\nand he who resorts in You finds refuge.\nوَ قَدْ لُذْتُ بِكَ يَآ اِلٰهِيْ فَلَا تُخَيِّبْ ظَنِّيْ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ\nWA QAD LUZTO BEKA YAA ELAAHEE FALAA TOKHAYYIB ZANNEE MIN RAHMATEKA\nIndeed certainly I have taken shelter in You, My Lord! So, (please) do not let down my opinion in Your mercy\nوَ لَا تَحْجُبْنِيْ عَنْ رَأْفَتِكَ\nWA LAA TAHJUBNEE A’N RAAFATEKA\nand do not exclude me from Your compassion.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اَقِمْنِيْ فِيْٓ اَهْلِ وِلَايَتِكَ\nELAAHEE AQIMNEE FEE AHLE WELAAYATEKA\nMy Lord, place me, among those who show servitude to You,\nمُقَامَ مَنْ رَجَا الزِّيَادَةَ مِنْ مَحَبَّتِكَ\nMOQAAMA MAN RAJAZ ZEYAADATA MIN MAHABBATEKA\nthe position of those who (incessantly) hope to increase Your love.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ اَلْهِمْنِيْ وَلَهًا بِذِكْرِكَ اِلٰى ذِكْرِكَ\nELAAHEE WA ALHIMNEE WALAHAN BE-ZIKREKA ELAA ZIKREKA\nMy Lord, (please) inspire me with a mounting passion for Your rememberance,\nوَ هِمَّتِيْ فِيْ رَوْحِ نَجَاحِ اَسْمَآئِكَ وَ مَحَلِّ قُدْسِكَ\nWA HIMMATEE FEE RAWHE NAJAAHE ASMAAA-EKA WA MAHALLE QUDSEKA\nand (please) with an ardour for the refreshing resort to Your names and the station of Your Holiness.\nاِلٰهِيْ بِكَ عَلَيْكَ اِلَّآ اَلْحَقْتَنِيْ بِمَحَلِّ اَهْلِ طَاعَتِكَ\nELAAHEE BEKA A’LAYKA ILLAA ALHAQTANEE BE-MAHALLE AHLE TAA-A’TEKA\nMy Lord, I beseech You in Your name to put me in the abode of those who are obedient to You\nوَ الْمَثْوَى الصَّالِحِ مِنْ مَرْضَاتِكَ\nWAL MASWAS SAALEHE MIN MARZAATEKA\nand to the righteous sanctuary of Your good pleasure,\nفَاِنِّيْ لَآ اَقْدِرُ لِنَفْسِيْ دَفْعًا\nFA-INNEE LAA AQDERO LE-NAFSEE DAF-A’N\nfor I, certainly have no power to repel any harm\nوَ لَا اَمْلِكُ لَهَا نَفْعًا\nWA LAA AMLEKO LAHAA NAF-A’N\nnor to obtain any benefit for it.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اَنَا عَبْدُكَ الضَّعِيْفُ الْمُذْنِبُ\nELAAHEE ANAA A’BDOKAZ ZA-E’EFUL MUZNEBO\nMy Lord, I am Your weak and sinful servant—\nوَ مَمْلُوْكُكَ الْمُنِيْبُ\nWA MAMLOOKOKAL MONEEBO\nand Your repenting slave.\nفَلا تَجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ صَرَفْتَ عَنْهُ وَجْهَكَ\nFA-LAA TAJ-A’LNEE MIMMAN SARAFTA A’NHO WAJHAKA\nSo, (please) do not include me amongst those from whom You have turned away Your face\nوَ حَجَبَهٗ سَهْوُهٗ عَنْ عَفْوِكَ\nWA HAJABAHU SAHWOHU A’N A’FWEKA\nand those who are excluded from Your pardon because of their lapses.\nاِلٰهِيْ هَبْ لِيْ كَمَالَ الْاِنْقِطَاعِ اِلَيْكَ\nELAAHEE HAB LEE KAMAALAL IN-QETAA-E’ ELAYKA\nMy Lord, (please) grant me absolute devotion to You\nوَ اَنِرْ اَبْصَارَ قُلُوْبِنَا بِضِيَآءِ نَظَرِهَآ اِلَيْكَ\nWA ANIR ABSAARE QOLOOBENAA BE-ZEYAAA-E NAZAREHAA ELAYKA\nand illumine the vision of our hearts by the light of their gaze looking towards You\nحَتّٰى تَخْرِقَ اَبْصَارُ الْقُلُوْبِ حُجُبَ النُّوْرِ\nHATTAA TAKHREQA ABSAARUL QOLOOBE HOJOBAN NOORE\nuntil the vision of our hearts pierces the curtains of light\nفَتَصِلَ اِلٰى مَعْدِنِ الْعَظَمَةِ\nFA-TASELA ELAA MA’DENIL A’ZAMATE\nto reach the core of supremacy,\nوَ تَصِيْرَ اَرْوَاحُنَا مُعَلَّقَةً بِعِزِّ قُدْسِكَ\nWA TASEERA ARWAAHONAA MO-A’LLAQATAN BE-I’ZZE QUDSEKA\nand that our souls become suspended by the majesty of Your Holiness.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ نَادَيْتَهٗ فَاَجَابَكَ\nELAAHEE WAJ A’LNEE MIMMAN NAADAYTAHU FA-AJAABAKA\nMy Lord, (please) appoint me of those who responded to You when You called them,\nوَ لَاحَظْتَهٗ فَصَعِقَ لِجَلَالِكَ\nWA LAA HAZTAHU FA-SA-E’QA LE-JALAALEKA\nand at whom You glanced so he swoons before Your Majesty\nفَنَاجَيْتَهٗ سِرًّا وَ عَمِلَ لَكَ جَهْرًا.\nFANAAJAYTAHU SIRRAN WA A’MELA LAKA JAHRAN\nSo You speak to him secretly and he works for You openly.\nاِلٰهِيْ لَمْ اُسَلِّطْ عَلٰى حُسْنِ ظَنِّيْ قُنُوْطَ الْاَيَاسِ\nELAAHEE LAM OSALLIT A’LAA HUSNE ZANNEE QONOOTAL AYAASE\nMy Lord, do not let the dejection of despair overshadow my beautiful opinion\nوَ لَا انْقَطَعَ رَجَآئِيْ مِنْ جَمِيْلِ كَرَمِكَ\nWA LAN QATA-A’ RAJAAA-EE MIN JAMEELE KARAMEKA\nand do not cut my hope from Your generosity\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ كَانَتِ الْخَطَايَا قَدْ اَسْقَطَتْنِيْ لَدَيْكَ\nELAAHEE IN KAANATIL KHATAAYAA QAD ASQATATNEE LADAYKA\nMy Lord, if my lapses have made me to fall from Your grace,\nفَاصْفَحْ عَنِّيْ بِحُسْنِ تَوَكُّلِيْ عَلَيْكَ\nFASFAH A’NNEE BE-HUSNE TAWAKKOLEE A’LAYKA\nSo please pardon me for the beauty of my reliance upon You.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ حَطَّتْنِيْ الذُّنُوْبُ مِنْ مَكَارِمِ لُطْفِكَ\nELAAHEE IN HATTAT-NIZ ZONOOBO MIN MAKAAREME LUTFEKA\nMy Lord, if my wrongdoings have excluded me from the generosity of Your grace,\nفَقَدْ نَبَّهَنِيْ الْيَقِيْنُ اِلٰى كَرَمِ عَطْفِكَ\nFAQAD NABBAHATNIL YAQEENO ELAA KARAME A’TFEKA\nSo certainly my conviction reassures me of Your generosity and gentleness.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ اَنَامَتْنِيْ الْغَفْلَةُ عَنِ الْاِسْتِعْدَادِ لِلِقَآئِكَ\nELAAHEE IN ANAA MATNIL GHAFLATO A’NIL ISTE’DAADE LE-LEQAAA-EKA\nMy Lord, if my neglect has lulled me into slumber preventing me from preparing myself for my meeting with You,\nفَقَدْ نَبَّهَتْنِي الْمَعْرِفَةُ بِكَرَمِ اٰلَآئِكَ\nFAQAD NABBA-HATNIL MA’REFATO BE-KARAME AALAAA-EKA\nSo certainly my recognition apprises me of your generous bounties has awakened me.\nاِلٰهِيْٓ اِنْ دَعَانِيْٓ اِلَى النَّارِ عَظِيْمُ عِقَابِكَ\nELAAHEE IN DA-A’AANEE ELAN NAARE A’ZEEMO E’QAABEKA\nMy Lord, if Your grave chastisement calls me to the Hellfire,\nفَقَدْ دَعَانِيْٓ اِلَى الْجَنَّةِ جَزِيْلُ ثَوَابِكَ\nFAQAD DA-A’AANEE ELAL JANNATE JAZEELO SAWAABEKA\nSo Your plentious reward has called me to Paradise.\nاِلٰهِيْ فَلَكَ اَسْاَلُ وَ اِلَيْكَ اَبْتَهِلُ وَ اَرْغَبُ\nELAAHEE FALAKA AS-ALO WA ELAYKA ABTAHELO WA ARGHABO\nMy Lord, so to You I beg and I implore and I request.\nوَ اَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA AS-ALOKA AN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nI beseech You to bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَ اَنْ تَجْعَلَنِيْ مِمَّنْ يُدِيْمُ ذِكْرَكَ\nWA AN TAJ-A’LANEE MIMMAN YODEEMO ZIKRAKA\nand to include me with those who always remember You,\nوَ لَا يَنْقُضُ عَهْدَكَ\nWA LAA YANQOZO A’HDAKA\nand those who never break their promise to You,\nوَ لَا يَغْفُلُ عَنْ شُكْرِكَ\nWA LAA YAGHFOLO A’N SHUKRAKA\nand who do not neglect to thank You,\nوَ لَا يَسْتَخِفُّ بِاَمْرِكَ\nWA LAA YASTAKHIFFO BE-AMREKA\nand who never belittle Your commands.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ اَلْحِقْنِيْ بِنُوْرِ عِزِّكَ الْاَبْهَجِ\nELAAHEE WA ALHIQNEE BE-NOORE I’ZZEKAL ABHAJE\nMy Lord, (please do) submerge me in the most blissful lights of Your majesty,\nفَاَكُوْنَ لَكَ عَارِفًا\nFA-AKOONA LAKA A’AREFAN\nso that I will recognize You\nوَ عَنْ سِوَاكَ مُنْحَرِفًا\nWA A’N SEWAAKA MUNHAREFAN\nand renounce all else except You,\nوَ مِنْكَ خَآئِفًا مُرَاقِبًا\nWA MINKA KHAA-EFAN MORAAQEBAN\nand that I will be fearful of and careful with You.\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME\nO Lord of Majesty and Honor!\nوَ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ رَسُوْلِهِ وَ اٰلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nWA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAA MOHAMMADIN RASOOLEHI WA AALEHIT TAAHEREENA\nMay Allah send blessings to Muhammad, His Messenger, and upon his Household the Infallible,\nوَ سَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا.\nWA SALLAMA TASLEEMAN 